  ],
  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "10",
      "part": "07",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m10p07-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "c19ea6971c460663be8e2396c60cc058b45f8677c5cf36bbf12f43d2ac8dcfc9",
        "2": "d4a84ada75b7662a901cd43c7617c34ea8eb45ed6830e6664ac5549c40a36409",
        "3": "8e454fcd2979afc0ce037c584825ad247095f8baeaf7558477b416e97abf9c48"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s01-c1-9c3222c3dc02",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "An E F S workload is quiet most of the day, then demand jumps. Which throughput mode fits? First separate throughput from performance mode. General Purpose is preferred for lower latency; Max I O is a previous-generation option with restrictions.",
          "text_sha256": "9c3222c3dc021bf6fda951866e0a553cee07b5ce6b8cee90e5d805423f537243",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8084f0951d79b76f6713ca866fe9784bbdfb5fb10480ebd83017a9317ba64abd",
          "asset_sha256": "c19ea6971c460663be8e2396c60cc058b45f8677c5cf36bbf12f43d2ac8dcfc9"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s01-c2-35b66532a501",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Follow the changing demand on the graph. Elastic throughput adapts as the work changes, so it can fit bursts you cannot predict. Client and service limits still matter.",
          "text_sha256": "35b66532a5017304138125ddbe2cf1e839231f8bcd59ded3e90643abc9306f66",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "35b66532a5017304138125ddbe2cf1e839231f8bcd59ded3e90643abc9306f66",
          "asset_sha256": "c19ea6971c460663be8e2396c60cc058b45f8677c5cf36bbf12f43d2ac8dcfc9"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s01-c3-04078682f346",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Provisioned throughput is a deliberate setting independent of stored capacity. Use it when you can estimate the throughput you need and want a defined setting instead of relying on storage-driven burst behavior.",
          "text_sha256": "04078682f3464a3d5b7aa17bc3be2d5d1d569dbf2ec1c865588439a2d2c7eb9d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "04078682f3464a3d5b7aa17bc3be2d5d1d569dbf2ec1c865588439a2d2c7eb9d",
          "asset_sha256": "c19ea6971c460663be8e2396c60cc058b45f8677c5cf36bbf12f43d2ac8dcfc9"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s01-c4-a3e7c08784f3",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "With Bursting, the data in Standard storage sets the baseline and credits. A job can finish a short spike and still run out of headroom in a long run. Check sustained demand and the credit balance.",
          "text_sha256": "a3e7c08784f34063bd55dd422a7dadc87002a705281f7bf57124645c362647fc",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a3e7c08784f34063bd55dd422a7dadc87002a705281f7bf57124645c362647fc",
          "asset_sha256": "c19ea6971c460663be8e2396c60cc058b45f8677c5cf36bbf12f43d2ac8dcfc9"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s02-c1-8024198aa9cf",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Several project files have gone quiet. The lifecycle clock follows time since file access, so files the app still opens can stay in Standard while inactive files qualify to move.",
          "text_sha256": "8024198aa9cf4e8ed5093809d484a3342f3fdbc11c8cc0bdda78988b94b2c617",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8024198aa9cf4e8ed5093809d484a3342f3fdbc11c8cc0bdda78988b94b2c617",
          "asset_sha256": "d4a84ada75b7662a901cd43c7617c34ea8eb45ed6830e6664ac5549c40a36409"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s02-c2-c88a2fa29eff",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A file can move to Infrequent Access after the configured inactivity period. The lower storage cost only helps if future reads are rare enough to justify the access charges and latency.",
          "text_sha256": "c88a2fa29eff1f6cb8fbe5038e40c434e6059d399631c829de9e100843c2f80f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c88a2fa29eff1f6cb8fbe5038e40c434e6059d399631c829de9e100843c2f80f",
          "asset_sha256": "d4a84ada75b7662a901cd43c7617c34ea8eb45ed6830e6664ac5549c40a36409"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s02-c3-167d2b8bc744",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For colder files, Archive adds a ninety-day minimum storage duration. It requires a Regional filesystem with Elastic throughput. A One Zone filesystem cannot use this class.",
          "text_sha256": "167d2b8bc7441c1d666b2e82616a572f8324f53163becff0e85c9f50210785bd",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "167d2b8bc7441c1d666b2e82616a572f8324f53163becff0e85c9f50210785bd",
          "asset_sha256": "d4a84ada75b7662a901cd43c7617c34ea8eb45ed6830e6664ac5549c40a36409"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s02-c4-73eea6981159",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "You can configure the first access to transition a file back to Standard. That makes sense when a formerly cold file is becoming active again. It is not a requirement to move a file before opening it.",
          "text_sha256": "73eea698115953899717dc2a71375b11d82920628f92c2b3c66f4fc7b0c55d73",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "73eea698115953899717dc2a71375b11d82920628f92c2b3c66f4fc7b0c55d73",
          "asset_sha256": "d4a84ada75b7662a901cd43c7617c34ea8eb45ed6830e6664ac5549c40a36409"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s03-c1-0632630cf131",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The source is still taking writes while E F S copies data asynchronously. After the first sync, you can read the destination, but it remains read-only under replication. Being able to read it does not tell you it's current.",
          "text_sha256": "0632630cf1310116682ba3ad70d418227d37bbb04979167acdf497067f6e305d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ee749357874ab0d4002ad85b8b1abed6b8f17775b4b48cf502f0bdd721b9b295",
          "asset_sha256": "8e454fcd2979afc0ce037c584825ad247095f8baeaf7558477b416e97abf9c48"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s03-c2-d20990b3ade6",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Check time since the last successful sync to estimate how much recent data may be at risk. Also prepare mount targets, application access, and key permissions. Replication lag and network readiness are separate checks.",
          "text_sha256": "d20990b3ade651037a4712b41b82b98a25dbc894a9f582e07e3d52786c263297",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d20990b3ade651037a4712b41b82b98a25dbc894a9f582e07e3d52786c263297",
          "asset_sha256": "8e454fcd2979afc0ce037c584825ad247095f8baeaf7558477b416e97abf9c48"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s03-c3-ce2d38e26ba9",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Before a planned switch, stop source writes and check the last successful sync. If an outage prevents that check, account for the lag rather than promising that every write survived.",
          "text_sha256": "ce2d38e26ba912d88ee9fe6ec6c36da933f4648f345cd7b5170c8bb088109317",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ce2d38e26ba912d88ee9fe6ec6c36da933f4648f345cd7b5170c8bb088109317",
          "asset_sha256": "8e454fcd2979afc0ce037c584825ad247095f8baeaf7558477b416e97abf9c48"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s03-c4-917a624bf8e8",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "For the depicted failover, delete the replication configuration and wait until the destination can accept writes. Do not direct a writer to a still read-only target.",
          "text_sha256": "917a624bf8e843d54f622f607e762a91e20e738e32921fa588922ce3b75e9a1d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "917a624bf8e843d54f622f607e762a91e20e738e32921fa588922ce3b75e9a1d",
          "asset_sha256": "8e454fcd2979afc0ce037c584825ad247095f8baeaf7558477b416e97abf9c48"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p07-andrew-exp-s03-c5-2afc7be6d895",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Now mount the writable destination and test a real application read and write. That proves the new path can serve the app; it does not give you point-in-time backup history.",
          "text_sha256": "2afc7be6d8951ecc7e92ea91d18304b85478dc5ee218e2a7fe1bd3d0f435dc27",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2afc7be6d8951ecc7e92ea91d18304b85478dc5ee218e2a7fe1bd3d0f435dc27",
          "asset_sha256": "8e454fcd2979afc0ce037c584825ad247095f8baeaf7558477b416e97abf9c48"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "10",
      "part": "08",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m10p08-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "ef8452087118ecc2cf131bfa77232ec07f62d5a23d02ae00695ad70259415699",
        "2": "36298308763435dc25af211521e4d18f6acadf3272acc006f77a387ff50aef75",
        "3": "11860b9896014baf9cbe26d6859829b16bfe56231262d3ae783749def58164c6",
        "4": "a8bcc03c4521d7293860113b6b49c0a3dc93beddf718bdbec9c48eb83e91cfea"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s01-c1-a9d8e82683d9",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Start with the client. If a Windows application needs an S M B share, Active Directory identities and Windows file permissions, F S x for Windows File Server fits that combination.",
          "text_sha256": "a9d8e82683d9dd1eefa835bac917ead2355fcb6776b161f694c5d2c41d497cb7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "252888279b2379e909ad380e45ed9b86b3ecbcfca1d6cea9eb08077e8f5fa8df",
          "asset_sha256": "ef8452087118ecc2cf131bfa77232ec07f62d5a23d02ae00695ad70259415699"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s01-c2-a6f1e3124abc",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A training job with many workers reading one dataset needs a different filesystem. Consider F S x for Lustre for high-performance parallel access with compatible Lustre clients. Link S three only where the deployment supports it.",
          "text_sha256": "a6f1e3124abcbb2a54dd9ea0fe8b2982c0e0e9b9c099546f496e01d904240b0a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c35f205cf17eb08ff8be4fa90698f205a04b4e77ded69cfd73b7d360681cf6e8",
          "asset_sha256": "ef8452087118ecc2cf131bfa77232ec07f62d5a23d02ae00695ad70259415699"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s01-c3-7cf0266c7971",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Use F S x for NetApp on tap when the design needs supported combinations of N F S, S M B, or eye scuzzy and on tap data features. A multi-protocol requirement is a different choice from Windows-only file sharing.",
          "text_sha256": "7cf0266c7971fe26dafe57e8e2228fcdf8ef754fbf6db7c89b1ff05140c31b7a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "cad85c95750e3614d8af3f21c167f11a004fafb05c1dd1ad0a429476c0ee3ef6",
          "asset_sha256": "ef8452087118ecc2cf131bfa77232ec07f62d5a23d02ae00695ad70259415699"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s01-c4-2563abab7853",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Use F S x for Open Z F S for Linux N F S workloads that need the Open Z F S model and features such as snapshots and clones. Compare the real client protocol and data operations before picking a family.",
          "text_sha256": "2563abab785356029c7e71fa0bac5298c8716d4bfc733fb1be07318b8384a13b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1a64d19c03b276d13aeda690e6ed4a654496a27a85ad0b9b3e7c26eb1630787f",
          "asset_sha256": "ef8452087118ecc2cf131bfa77232ec07f62d5a23d02ae00695ad70259415699"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s02-c1-fe173376b571",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The Windows or compatible S M B client connects to the file system over T C P port four forty-five, using the share path. A failure to reach that port is a network problem to diagnose before changing permissions.",
          "text_sha256": "fe173376b5713d80ed29a1d53eb4cfdf53c41fdafbf7c0b04b7e891025010e73",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "96ed06148188e3c4e58deb0531ef501bd9d0a35666a412ffa3bf85525be89d88",
          "asset_sha256": "36298308763435dc25af211521e4d18f6acadf3272acc006f77a387ff50aef75"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s02-c2-f3e718af02f6",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Active Directory supplies the identities and groups used for authorization. An authenticated user still needs permission on both the share and the file or folder.",
          "text_sha256": "f3e718af02f66ec7393cdef3ba9a3c992723cd6b52afb1e13a86054ddbce17d1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f3e718af02f66ec7393cdef3ba9a3c992723cd6b52afb1e13a86054ddbce17d1",
          "asset_sha256": "36298308763435dc25af211521e4d18f6acadf3272acc006f77a387ff50aef75"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s02-c3-17f37c4b114c",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Alice has Change on the share and Modify on the file. Both allow the operation in this example, so her update can succeed.",
          "text_sha256": "17f37c4b114c584827b4a31785206c6699c4004ae8878dfebaaa46bee5f3e628",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "17f37c4b114c584827b4a31785206c6699c4004ae8878dfebaaa46bee5f3e628",
          "asset_sha256": "36298308763435dc25af211521e4d18f6acadf3272acc006f77a387ff50aef75"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s02-c4-431f890ac1fc",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Now compare Bob. The file permissions say Modify, but the share grants only Read. Over the share, he can read the file but not modify it. Setting the file permission alone did not give him Alice's result.",
          "text_sha256": "431f890ac1fc733e357563a40afbaa2a1214e4e3b71caf6138ae664795f9f306",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "431f890ac1fc733e357563a40afbaa2a1214e4e3b71caf6138ae664795f9f306",
          "asset_sha256": "36298308763435dc25af211521e4d18f6acadf3272acc006f77a387ff50aef75"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s02-c5-907ce771c689",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For a failed connection, verify name resolution, routing and the security group allowing S M B traffic. An on-premises client also needs a working private path such as V P N or Direct Connect.",
          "text_sha256": "907ce771c68994eae7cf5829bc4448a38163426f549dd393ba8fede530a96c32",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0bb0333053ac8d23cee2c84696f5cf89acd1d35868752df6e22ee7c264486e68",
          "asset_sha256": "36298308763435dc25af211521e4d18f6acadf3272acc006f77a387ff50aef75"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s03-c1-7263c7902417",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Before failover, the Windows client uses the F S x D N S name to reach the preferred active server. The Multi-AZ file system synchronously replicates to the standby in another zone.",
          "text_sha256": "7263c79024173aebdbe43cde68aae07a828b5dda3ce8b8e149e61dcd454d015d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9fc925c77c02bb4cb39e1487881f19009c25e73064031a41320735b9e8643166",
          "asset_sha256": "11860b9896014baf9cbe26d6859829b16bfe56231262d3ae783749def58164c6"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s03-c2-803d9e7fdb17",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "When the preferred server fails, the other server takes over reads and writes. Windows clients use the same D N S name and can resume after a brief interruption. Don't tie them to the old server's I P address.",
          "text_sha256": "803d9e7fdb17bc53e43d8f6f4608a9d5b7c63e3aab9b5f5b47e44feea2165d96",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d6c1404cd44c40ba30725ebaeb10002deebcf00e13e95aa891238e0683641d0f",
          "asset_sha256": "11860b9896014baf9cbe26d6859829b16bfe56231262d3ae783749def58164c6"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s03-c3-79dfa1b20041",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Same D N S name does not guarantee the same recovery behavior for all clients. Linux clients do not automatically follow this D N S-based failover; test how your client reconnects.",
          "text_sha256": "79dfa1b200416874ede7f6ac25a5d0f89735a62318e0e14195b61277626515c8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1fc2972fbe3f659489bba07499d616819668f281b9517a4ce6a71f459f28fc52",
          "asset_sha256": "11860b9896014baf9cbe26d6859829b16bfe56231262d3ae783749def58164c6"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s03-c4-8feb80918f07",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "But will the standby bring back an accidentally deleted file? No. Failover helps when the server is unavailable. Recover deleted data from an earlier backup rather than treating the standby as history.",
          "text_sha256": "8feb80918f075e32a051a4a742d0e138e4fd6d955dada2c66d8316b223496da1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8feb80918f075e32a051a4a742d0e138e4fd6d955dada2c66d8316b223496da1",
          "asset_sha256": "11860b9896014baf9cbe26d6859829b16bfe56231262d3ae783749def58164c6"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s04-c1-3ca3cb41bc0d",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "You need to move a Windows share without losing who can open it. Inventory the source paths, identities and access controls first. Those become the checks for the new share.",
          "text_sha256": "3ca3cb41bc0db2f767be8e455f04fa560edc2ffd0c63f77c7fda45f5fa578219",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3ca3cb41bc0db2f767be8e455f04fa560edc2ffd0c63f77c7fda45f5fa578219",
          "asset_sha256": "a8bcc03c4521d7293860113b6b49c0a3dc93beddf718bdbec9c48eb83e91cfea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s04-c2-def8e6e87d7b",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Prepare the new F S x target, join it to the intended directory as appropriate, and verify connectivity and access against a representative client before the cutover.",
          "text_sha256": "def8e6e87d7bf9fe52ee21fd5aeffc767541f09b8efdfcd4373ca87f199c2a09",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a7b0ad870b6aa11fe5c5a2941caf81855030633c6673a27214aae283ca7e5fcc",
          "asset_sha256": "a8bcc03c4521d7293860113b6b49c0a3dc93beddf718bdbec9c48eb83e91cfea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s04-c3-1af393dcab26",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Copy the data using a supported method such as DataSync or Robocopy. Preserve the required security metadata and check that the files and permissions at the destination match what the workload needs.",
          "text_sha256": "1af393dcab266683adcb2963f730d0222120b7ddd4287af4b511dd93d7e26619",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1af393dcab266683adcb2963f730d0222120b7ddd4287af4b511dd93d7e26619",
          "asset_sha256": "a8bcc03c4521d7293860113b6b49c0a3dc93beddf718bdbec9c48eb83e91cfea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s04-c4-5445675364cb",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Let users keep working on the source during the bulk copy. At the final sync, pause source writes and copy what changed. Then you can switch without leaving the newest writes behind.",
          "text_sha256": "5445675364cb7d8ac0560e40c8926b0a42e3ff3f7eab6b3d914d543fd51b0be0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5445675364cb7d8ac0560e40c8926b0a42e3ff3f7eab6b3d914d543fd51b0be0",
          "asset_sha256": "a8bcc03c4521d7293860113b6b49c0a3dc93beddf718bdbec9c48eb83e91cfea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s04-c5-add493b87570",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Switch the client paths and test from the application and a representative user's account. A file listing from the migration operator does not prove the right users can open the files.",
          "text_sha256": "add493b875701c4fb83667a8796e75ca134d3dec9b0f8b1a28d229aee67d01d0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "add493b875701c4fb83667a8796e75ca134d3dec9b0f8b1a28d229aee67d01d0",
          "asset_sha256": "a8bcc03c4521d7293860113b6b49c0a3dc93beddf718bdbec9c48eb83e91cfea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p08-andrew-exp-s04-c6-525e9c9ce7e6",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "If the requirement is a smaller file system, copy into a new, appropriately sized target. Restoring a backup does not shrink the allocated capacity.",
          "text_sha256": "525e9c9ce7e609a73a688e045918b53b7fe4933ea7a2774da1697c05034f1727",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "525e9c9ce7e609a73a688e045918b53b7fe4933ea7a2774da1697c05034f1727",
          "asset_sha256": "a8bcc03c4521d7293860113b6b49c0a3dc93beddf718bdbec9c48eb83e91cfea"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "10",
      "part": "09",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m10p09-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "4c2bae6161a900a257dcd25d63d8a6c674b7825ecef8e479323d3cfeb804d2a8",
        "2": "81c24b415df78516205bed19bdfea6b94b0cab3bbc6a70645399c614c7c91dea",
        "3": "211cc35ae9db93e6be52721ad8be2c299384cc6b70dd7c7ab829774672797c3b"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s01-c1-46958470da86",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A training job has many workers but only one dataset. Instead of copying the whole dataset to every host, use compatible Lustre clients to read from one shared filesystem.",
          "text_sha256": "46958470da86dbfafd17f4349a24a8256e1f3978be4d042e986b638686307411",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "46958470da86dbfafd17f4349a24a8256e1f3978be4d042e986b638686307411",
          "asset_sha256": "4c2bae6161a900a257dcd25d63d8a6c674b7825ecef8e479323d3cfeb804d2a8"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s01-c2-e247218d9fce",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "F S x for Lustre presents the shared high-performance filesystem.",
          "text_sha256": "e247218d9fceedeb50abfdddc4f1d6bb39f85cbe9a52b1be2e5c982f978aa6b6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "20bc01486753bff2eb8b6aed4be7da44761a7cebbce7a6815eebdb70a8d546a8",
          "asset_sha256": "4c2bae6161a900a257dcd25d63d8a6c674b7825ecef8e479323d3cfeb804d2a8"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s01-c3-a849e76c0a73",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "If the input starts in S three, link it on a supported Lustre configuration. The workers still open files through Lustre. Configure and verify export if the results need to end up back in S three.",
          "text_sha256": "a849e76c0a734eb745bc5acde3bbe5aa9d3e076a7e0a8f38e8827524554110db",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "eff95f51cf766473111febe94807828e6d4ddec696e729c725b5b0ac6926fb8b",
          "asset_sha256": "4c2bae6161a900a257dcd25d63d8a6c674b7825ecef8e479323d3cfeb804d2a8"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s01-c4-106c4f8b6c10",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Size for the actual job: many small files can put pressure on metadata operations even when bulk throughput looks adequate. Measure open and lookup activity as well as the data rate.",
          "text_sha256": "106c4f8b6c10642fb707128e01574542f5a4e83041740f8252a75b76f8635ab7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "106c4f8b6c10642fb707128e01574542f5a4e83041740f8252a75b76f8635ab7",
          "asset_sha256": "4c2bae6161a900a257dcd25d63d8a6c674b7825ecef8e479323d3cfeb804d2a8"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s02-c1-3bfbcd9915b4",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Ask what happens to the job if a component fails. Scratch does not replicate the data; choose it for work you can rerun and keep indispensable inputs or outputs elsewhere.",
          "text_sha256": "3bfbcd9915b4665d1c451bc896ee97a048d498e3679b98b7acb34f6c73c05abd",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3bfbcd9915b4665d1c451bc896ee97a048d498e3679b98b7acb34f6c73c05abd",
          "asset_sha256": "81c24b415df78516205bed19bdfea6b94b0cab3bbc6a70645399c614c7c91dea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s02-c2-be5e0f7cb263",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Persistent S S D and H D D protect data with replication within one Availability Zone and replace failed components. That makes them a better fit for longer-running work, but it does not make this a multi-zone data copy.",
          "text_sha256": "be5e0f7cb2631ffa64d4d3b29b55a6d2e22aea7eeb4e66e780bcff18e3c00782",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "98578126ac0c984acf9002ddf0681307f9e32165beffb400a1e58da225211f49",
          "asset_sha256": "81c24b415df78516205bed19bdfea6b94b0cab3bbc6a70645399c614c7c91dea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s02-c3-87e571a02954",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Intelligent-Tiering replicates data across zones. That's about where copies live, not a promise that clients never lose service. This storage class also cannot link to an S three data repository.",
          "text_sha256": "87e571a029544d249bb6f06c7e6f375fb1affae623b88d729feb8cd8ffe2e09b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7157ec00a5e1605742037f7b62e54bad8a4465f2eca6c97bd16be2d1a5ab2699",
          "asset_sha256": "81c24b415df78516205bed19bdfea6b94b0cab3bbc6a70645399c614c7c91dea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s03-c1-e7de834f9e04",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Start by associating an S three bucket or prefix with a Lustre directory on a supported deployment and version. An unavailable repository feature is a configuration mismatch, not a missing file.",
          "text_sha256": "e7de834f9e04d05b92b55e0c2c0291e2b94b727299d22e97b5770b77e49d704c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8385635608cd9f25e535f47aae7eb2d5732b5c2cb3adf841025f786765d8be78",
          "asset_sha256": "211cc35ae9db93e6be52721ad8be2c299384cc6b70dd7c7ab829774672797c3b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s03-c2-afd5328ea50f",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The directory lists the filenames and sizes after the metadata arrives. Does that mean the bytes are already on the filesystem? Not necessarily. The listing can be ready before the contents.",
          "text_sha256": "afd5328ea50fff9d8042b682733ecf79191a0961e2c01f2101c183a1eef1df2c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "afd5328ea50fff9d8042b682733ecf79191a0961e2c01f2101c183a1eef1df2c",
          "asset_sha256": "211cc35ae9db93e6be52721ad8be2c299384cc6b70dd7c7ab829774672797c3b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s03-c3-8a887c37bcc7",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The worker opens the four-hundred-fifty-megabyte file. That first read can trigger loading its bytes from S three, so budget for the time even though the name was there already.",
          "text_sha256": "8a887c37bcc78b7312ee9cfb237ea197ba39b77d63373279c45bacb0fe840344",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "95376889fb8002cded687be3a6f20944095421f45c2bb4c10a0951f2257bfc83",
          "asset_sha256": "211cc35ae9db93e6be52721ad8be2c299384cc6b70dd7c7ab829774672797c3b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s03-c4-dc6b12bdc902",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The workers process files through Lustre. Once required content is present, later access need not pay the same initial loading delay.",
          "text_sha256": "dc6b12bdc9028ced5fd32f6cc8b339529c366b6552719f6e584fc2e8d1b8ee4a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "dc6b12bdc9028ced5fd32f6cc8b339529c366b6552719f6e584fc2e8d1b8ee4a",
          "asset_sha256": "211cc35ae9db93e6be52721ad8be2c299384cc6b70dd7c7ab829774672797c3b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p09-andrew-exp-s03-c5-621244db2d6d",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The new output is now a Lustre file. Run the configured export or a repository task and check that the object arrived in S three before relying on that copy.",
          "text_sha256": "621244db2d6d7f921be6a6e403bf0fe2ab8adaab2dda063330a248348068b374",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4013a0aa0e2a5cecbc56cba4fe6fe18fe1aa4ba5524bdd824b266c4b73c2ec1d",
          "asset_sha256": "211cc35ae9db93e6be52721ad8be2c299384cc6b70dd7c7ab829774672797c3b"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "10",
      "part": "10",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m10p10-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "2486ddecdbee64ab5944232b1a244b72574714147ab81e5653ae56f4a43426be",
        "2": "d9c83e97e5a7139c379547572b76d17d0168fb472519fd30151ac739a8c2b160"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m10p10-andrew-exp-s01-c1-1bf85a465915",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Two clients ask for files by name. The N F S and S M B clients use file endpoints on the on tap storage virtual machine. They go to a file volume, not to raw blocks.",
          "text_sha256": "1bf85a4659150299b4f63ded003d19508f417c0700ffec2fffda040dccf54808",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e1f33fa543f0c51ac0915810397ca5e2d6e9d069742135552ec6561274369092",
          "asset_sha256": "2486ddecdbee64ab5944232b1a244b72574714147ab81e5653ae56f4a43426be"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p10-andrew-exp-s01-c2-dfc2c24ba7c7",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The eye scuzzy client asks for a logical unit instead. It sees a block device. That is why it cannot browse the S M B share through the same interface.",
          "text_sha256": "dfc2c24ba7c724ece9320202497c9246faec3dceba95413fb9c3c4b20c8a7ea3",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "450e6285413662ee2246b147a807104db6d92a5e02c75f8f2e80e949909d1bc8",
          "asset_sha256": "2486ddecdbee64ab5944232b1a244b72574714147ab81e5653ae56f4a43426be"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p10-andrew-exp-s01-c3-373e3a05f841",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "on tap offers features such as snapshots, clones, compression and deduplication. These help manage data and copies, but they do not turn every write or copy into zero-cost storage.",
          "text_sha256": "373e3a05f841f3ef0133ee7ec8d64f0f8e6bb03a5edb86e577e0b862c2893add",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0fdb83e3f119cf26d451c4c2261e6c75834febab7a6fecf6d22aa2eddb427b2a",
          "asset_sha256": "2486ddecdbee64ab5944232b1a244b72574714147ab81e5653ae56f4a43426be"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p10-andrew-exp-s01-c4-aa534bf722e9",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Account for S S D capacity, I ops and throughput as well as tiering. New writes still consume space; using a data-efficiency feature is not a substitute for sizing.",
          "text_sha256": "aa534bf722e9a973a5ce2b008a0d2cecddadee6a120d5d8528a1d864567d04ac",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1e4a5a6a544a2aaf036e942753e9839770ec9abc0da875f7c74a5eae16782c89",
          "asset_sha256": "2486ddecdbee64ab5944232b1a244b72574714147ab81e5653ae56f4a43426be"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p10-andrew-exp-s02-c1-5659b51d8665",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Open Z F S serves the source volume to N F S clients. The snapshot and clone use that same dataset as a starting point, but serve two different purposes.",
          "text_sha256": "5659b51d866523ecc4ad546ef50c96aaffebefd52195a40673a0e0e97e18e36b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1be7aa2e1c9d1bc720872bfca332cc6496a3a73a14501d910ee641423935c37c",
          "asset_sha256": "d9c83e97e5a7139c379547572b76d17d0168fb472519fd30151ac739a8c2b160"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p10-andrew-exp-s02-c2-7187a6f5fc35",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A snapshot captures the source volume at a point in time. The captured data is read-only, so a test cannot change that state directly.",
          "text_sha256": "7187a6f5fc3599ce46a4eea1d8f903e0b7fd4e1c6950cd9a747ab1e9c6999643",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7187a6f5fc3599ce46a4eea1d8f903e0b7fd4e1c6950cd9a747ab1e9c6999643",
          "asset_sha256": "d9c83e97e5a7139c379547572b76d17d0168fb472519fd30151ac739a8c2b160"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p10-andrew-exp-s02-c3-027ff5337aa8",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Create a writable clone and point the test at it. Changes consume capacity, and the clone still depends on its source snapshot. An independent full copy is a different choice.",
          "text_sha256": "027ff5337aa82b14a8a8c0f2bfe28b3840a7ba7c80da67493d0a67b2e2c16940",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "027ff5337aa82b14a8a8c0f2bfe28b3840a7ba7c80da67493d0a67b2e2c16940",
          "asset_sha256": "d9c83e97e5a7139c379547572b76d17d0168fb472519fd30151ac739a8c2b160"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p10-andrew-exp-s02-c4-9ab48358cf64",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Choose the deployment availability and throughput independently from how you will create test copies. A clone within the same system is convenient for parallel work, but it does not isolate that work from loss of the filesystem.",
          "text_sha256": "9ab48358cf647e9ead2aaba7101eb884525d8b4195ea6065870e13c4fe662ace",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9ab48358cf647e9ead2aaba7101eb884525d8b4195ea6065870e13c4fe662ace",
          "asset_sha256": "d9c83e97e5a7139c379547572b76d17d0168fb472519fd30151ac739a8c2b160"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "10",
      "part": "11",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m10p11-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "6047532046465071639e6bca7096f519a7155c84584802c1e63587e4eb874dbd",
        "2": "5e2efb386f1d839e5845b502c17c141ebfb71375af08aa59b5f30fdfc6d9f87d",
        "3": "e8454c52ff421a9a8820fdd0ddb9c79a75167873b9730b838c5a45ddc47ff0e9"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m10p11-andrew-exp-s01-c1-c33ab3672e74",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A local app still wants an N F S or S M B file path, but the data needs to land in S three. File Gateway sits between them: the app uses files, and the gateway handles the object uploads.",
          "text_sha256": "c33ab3672e747d7edce4e9016a86f84c95b58c250317482acfaa6a1a2261023a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3f63cdd2d2264585e385a112e45173fbbae264c5e2ccddbf012a6289f19bcabc",
          "asset_sha256": "6047532046465071639e6bca7096f519a7155c84584802c1e63587e4eb874dbd"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p11-andrew-exp-s01-c2-90810ce9c448",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The backend is S three object storage. Uploads from the gateway are asynchronous, so a successful local write is not proof that the corresponding S three object has already arrived.",
          "text_sha256": "90810ce9c4489f3b75490ae842f1198db85e279d0536c004960e77fdbe5dab82",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2acd07b96e6227490af9e3163e3fe88926b28c7c54857edfabbdb555927bb2f7",
          "asset_sha256": "6047532046465071639e6bca7096f519a7155c84584802c1e63587e4eb874dbd"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p11-andrew-exp-s01-c3-a6095d6a301e",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A local client can read cached data without waiting for another S three fetch. On a cache miss, the gateway must retrieve the required data, so the cloud path still matters.",
          "text_sha256": "a6095d6a301e443b45be439d5b4ab8528ac25e609bf3e6f316ca302312357914",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4f4886c3b189dd12e71313e96b4981fdb5678bbfa684e061e4369364afe3e1e4",
          "asset_sha256": "6047532046465071639e6bca7096f519a7155c84584802c1e63587e4eb874dbd"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p11-andrew-exp-s01-c4-67f8671bb0bb",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Follow one report write. The gateway updates its local cache and uploads the object afterward. A successful local write does not yet prove that the object arrived in S three.",
          "text_sha256": "67f8671bb0bb286fec8ffa1424b4beb8e535ab04c4f4fcd528b2a78564b92fe8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c418de72f7221fcfb5c105431790eca48df56afaa9058fc085b5cc0e5016d289",
          "asset_sha256": "6047532046465071639e6bca7096f519a7155c84584802c1e63587e4eb874dbd"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p11-andrew-exp-s01-c5-a1db81e0e09e",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "If a separate authorized process updates the bucket, the gateway can keep showing old metadata. Refresh its cached inventory if needed so clients discover the new object. That does not settle competing writes.",
          "text_sha256": "a1db81e0e09ebbe383e0d360f6efc392dd8c1846021c6799bb3d1843e3a8ae22",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a1db81e0e09ebbe383e0d360f6efc392dd8c1846021c6799bb3d1843e3a8ae22",
          "asset_sha256": "6047532046465071639e6bca7096f519a7155c84584802c1e63587e4eb874dbd"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p11-andrew-exp-s02-c1-0a07ac626efc",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For a cached volume, the app attaches an eye scuzzy block device while the primary data lives in A W S. Keep cache and an upload buffer locally; you do not need room for the entire primary volume.",
          "text_sha256": "0a07ac626efce89d477e15a9a87b635481ce8abe3efbf653131c3feefefeb61b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6829424884c3a0c58251ddd44d2c65aeb2f6fc3e5ecb917e7f9143286a6cea8a",
          "asset_sha256": "5e2efb386f1d839e5845b502c17c141ebfb71375af08aa59b5f30fdfc6d9f87d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p11-andrew-exp-s02-c2-77df231d2c36",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Stored mode reverses the placement: the complete primary volume stays local, and snapshots go to A W S asynchronously. Choose it when the workload needs that local copy and you can supply all its capacity.",
          "text_sha256": "77df231d2c36752b94fb05518de438d917972423b6d13fa29daf244abba65268",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ddd3bf98fff8bc99f76b252c53839d6407e74e6589fe19bbbfd7fd99f5e61a77",
          "asset_sha256": "5e2efb386f1d839e5845b502c17c141ebfb71375af08aa59b5f30fdfc6d9f87d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p11-andrew-exp-s03-c1-419ea0b975bd",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The backup application connects over eye scuzzy to a virtual tape library. It can keep its tape workflow while writing to a virtual tape rather than a physical cartridge.",
          "text_sha256": "419ea0b975bd1938d96ca6f32dea9991121487c7ccfc6e230c7398bb0781bb82",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c92a7fc4beb15a8d663338238d2dfd9ce9322afb076a0220ac9ade63d6f5cd4a",
          "asset_sha256": "e8454c52ff421a9a8820fdd0ddb9c79a75167873b9730b838c5a45ddc47ff0e9"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p11-andrew-exp-s03-c2-486dac47f4fc",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "On the gateway, online tapes are backed by S three. Ejecting a tape can put it in the configured archive. It will no longer behave like an online tape immediately available for a restore.",
          "text_sha256": "486dac47f4fc0df168ce21a67c5026b1bef8ae14d62a532711f83bd46e41537a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a76453a47da7f9e5cccea4833a44262f939bb41f3332fe225aba4e2229dec80e",
          "asset_sha256": "e8454c52ff421a9a8820fdd0ddb9c79a75167873b9730b838c5a45ddc47ff0e9"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p11-andrew-exp-s03-c3-ade07599e24b",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "You need the archived backup now. First retrieve the virtual tape to the gateway. Only then can the backup program read it, so plan for retrieval time and charges before committing to the recovery deadline.",
          "text_sha256": "ade07599e24b55a1daf174f530ecd1fc95746c8f3b481be2d903aa571d610ff7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ade07599e24b55a1daf174f530ecd1fc95746c8f3b481be2d903aa571d610ff7",
          "asset_sha256": "e8454c52ff421a9a8820fdd0ddb9c79a75167873b9730b838c5a45ddc47ff0e9"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
